{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-86-r2-holdout/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"text": "Excellent! All acceptance criteria are met. Now let me commit the fix:", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CfV9eGaZWTCPpWGq685Bx", "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "3e51e9aa-e1c9-492d-89dd-4548622c26fc", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:45:24.628Z", "type": "assistant"}
{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-86-r2-holdout/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"id": "toolu_0161iBwSaWZ3gwiMnvqCrVvN", "input": {"command": "git add src/cargo/hazmat.ts && git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nFix segregation check for hazmat classes with divisions\n\nThe mustSegregate function was incorrectly using only the primary class (e.g.,\n\"5\" from \"5.1\") for lookups, but the segregation table contains entries with\ndivisions (e.g., \"5.1\", \"5.2\"). This caused hazmat classes like oxidisers and\norganic peroxides to never match, allowing dangerous incompatibilities.\n\nNow uses the full class string for table lookups to correctly identify\nsegregation requirements between all hazmat classes including those with\ndivisions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\""}, "name": "Bash", "type": "tool_use"}], "id": "msg_011CfV9eGaZWTCPpWGq685Bx", "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "3e51e9aa-e1c9-492d-89dd-4548622c26fc", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:45:26.994Z", "type": "assistant"}
