{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch/runs/eval-INC-86-r2-holdout/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"text": "Done! I've fixed INC-86. \n\nThe issue was that the segregation check was using only the primary class (e.g., \"5\" from \"5.1\") for lookups, but the segregation table contains entries with full classes including divisions (e.g., \"5.1\", \"5.2\"). This meant hazmat classes with divisions were never matched, allowing dangerous incompatibilities like explosives next to oxidisers.\n\nThe fix updates `mustSegregate()` to use the full class string for table lookups, ensuring all hazmat classes—including those with divisions like oxidisers (5.1) and organic peroxides (5.2)—are properly validated against segregation rules. All tests pass and the acceptance criteria are met.", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CfV9eY9wfT5t2A7J9eFkD", "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "3e51e9aa-e1c9-492d-89dd-4548622c26fc", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:45:30.010Z", "type": "assistant"}
